# predatorctl-restore.service preferences.
#
# You normally don't need to touch this file: predatorctl-helper writes
# /etc/predatorctl/restore.conf itself, automatically, every time you change
# a setting (thermal profile, RGB effect, battery limiter, fan) in the app --
# so your last values are already reapplied at the next boot with zero setup.
#
# This example is here for the manual case: adding an entry the app doesn't
# cover, or seeding a value before ever launching the GUI. To use it, copy
# it to /etc/predatorctl/restore.conf (root-owned, not user-writable) and
# uncomment/edit the lines you want -- predatorctl-helper will preserve your
# comments and just update its own lines going forward.
#
# One "action=value" pair per line, same action names and value formats as
# the pkexec helper (see helper/predatorctl-helper ACTIONS/validate(), and
# "Value formats" in CLAUDE.md). Blank lines and lines starting with '#'
# are ignored. Invalid lines/values are skipped with a warning in the
# journal (`journalctl -u predatorctl-restore`), never fatal to the rest.

# platform_profile=balanced-performance
# battery_limiter=1
# lcd_override=0
# fan_speed=0,0
# four_zone_mode=1,4,100,1,0,255,120
